        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 163.933,
          "en": "the UserProfile component which has some dummy output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 168.19,
          "en": "So we have a brand new state to manage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.19,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "And unlike the counter state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 173.13,
          "en": "which was just a basic example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.13,
          "end": 175.54,
          "en": "the authentication state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.54,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "and the answer to the question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 180.24,
          "en": "whether the user is logged in or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.24,
          "end": 182.87,
          "en": "is indeed not just local state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.87,
          "end": 186.47,
          "en": "which matters to one specific component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.47,
          "end": 189.13,
          "en": "but it is application-wide state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.13,
          "end": 193.2,
          "en": "which matters to a lot of components in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.2,
          "end": 194.68,
          "en": "It matters to the Header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.68,
          "end": 196.48,
          "en": "it matters to the Auth component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.48,
          "end": 199.693,
          "en": "it matters to the UserProfile component in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.89,
          "end": 205.09,
          "en": "So therefore, this is the user authenticated state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.09,
          "end": 207.73,
          "en": "is a perfect example for a state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.73,
          "end": 211.12,
          "en": "that we could manage with React context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.12,
          "end": 215.13,
          "en": "or since this section is about Redux, with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.13,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "And that's therefore what I wanna do now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 220.51,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that when we click the Login button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.51,
          "end": 224.1,
          "en": "we set the user to authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.1,
          "end": 226.03,
          "en": "If we click the Logout button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.03,
          "end": 229.94,
          "en": "I wanna set the user to not authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.94,
          "end": 232.53,
          "en": "And for this, in our store here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.53,
          "end": 234.98,
          "en": "we can add a brand new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.98,
          "end": 237.003,
          "en": "a brand new piece of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.63,
          "end": 239.53,
          "en": "Now, the question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.53,
          "end": 244.37,
          "en": "is where we should add our authentication data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.37,
          "end": 247.32,
          "en": "We do have this slice, which we created here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.32,
          "end": 249.29,
          "en": "this counter slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.29,
          "end": 250.96,
          "en": "and in there, we manage the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.96,
          "end": 253.223,
          "en": "and the showCounter state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.07,
          "end": 257.27,
          "en": "We could, of course, also add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.27,
          "end": 259.12,
          "en": "to our state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.12,
          "end": 263.86,
          "en": "Let's say the isAuthenticated property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.86,
          "end": 265.83,
          "en": "and set this to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.83,
          "end": 270.37,
          "en": "and then add a new reducer, login, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.37,
          "end": 272.09000000000003,
          "en": "a new reducer method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.09000000000003,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "and in here, we then set is isAuthenticated to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "We could do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 280.27,
          "en": "but logically it makes no sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.27,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "The authentication status has nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 284.83,
          "en": "to do with the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.83,
          "end": 287.22,
          "en": "Whilst it would technically work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.22,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "in programming we typically wanna separate our concerns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 295.88,
          "en": "We wanna make sure that this slice really focuses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.88,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "on the counter-related state and actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 304.16,
          "en": "And we should create a brand new slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.16,
          "end": 306.703,
          "en": "for the authentication state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.6,
          "end": 309.78,
          "en": "And that's, therefore, what I'll do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.78,
          "end": 312.06,
          "en": "I'll rename this initialState up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.06,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "to the initialCounterState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.45,
          "end": 318.36,
          "en": "because we will soon have more than one initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.7,
          "end": 323.59,
          "en": "and therefore, I set the initialState property in this slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 323.59,
          "end": 327.42,
          "en": "to the value stored in initialCounterState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.42,
          "end": 329.93,
          "en": "And then we can add a new slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.93,
          "end": 332.72,
          "en": "below the other slice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.72,
          "end": 336.11,
          "en": "though the exact position does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 336.11,
          "end": 338.822,
          "en": "But we can call createSlice again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.822,
          "end": 340.72,
          "en": "to create another slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.72,
          "end": 344.4,
          "en": "and this slice also, of course, needs an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 347.86,
          "en": "to be configured, just as our first slice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.86,
          "end": 350.88,
          "en": "This slice will be configured in exactly the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.88,
          "end": 353.33,
          "en": "just with different values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.33,
          "end": 354.71,
          "en": "So we add a name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.71,
          "end": 358.81,
          "en": "and set this to auth, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 358.81,
          "end": 362.5,
          "en": "or authentication, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 362.5,
          "end": 366.42,
          "en": "And we also wanna assign some initialState here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.42,
          "end": 368.78,
          "en": "Now, we could create this on the fly here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.78,
          "end": 370.88,
          "en": "or again create a separate constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.88,
          "end": 372.703,
          "en": "which holds this initial state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.703,
          "end": 374.5,
          "en": "and that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.5,
          "end": 376.853,
          "en": "I'll add a const initialAuthState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 378.77,
          "end": 380.96,
          "en": "which again let's say is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 380.96,
          "end": 384.32,
          "en": "where we have the isAuthenticated property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 384.32,
          "end": 387.11,
          "en": "which initially is set to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 387.11,
          "end": 389.08,
          "en": "And then here I set initialState equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 389.08,
          "end": 391.493,
          "en": "to this initialAuthState value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.58,
          "end": 395.96,
          "en": "And then we need to register our reducers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.96,
          "end": 400.18,
          "en": "These reducer methods, which can change this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 400.18,
          "end": 403.89,
          "en": "And here I think two methods make sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 403.89,
          "end": 408.21,
          "en": "A login method for well, logging the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 408.21,
          "end": 412.05,
          "en": "And a logout method for logging the user out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 412.05,
          "end": 415.45,
          "en": "In both methods, we'll receive the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 415.45,
          "end": 420.4,
          "en": "as an argument automatically provided by Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.4,
          "end": 423.92,
          "en": "and we can then mutate this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 423.92,
          "end": 425.87,
          "en": "even though we technically shouldn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 425.87,
          "end": 428.09,
          "en": "but as I explained, we can do it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 428.09,
          "end": 429.7,
          "en": "because under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 429.7,
          "end": 433.82,
          "en": "our code will be transformed to actually not mutate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 433.82,
          "end": 434.94,
          "en": "the original state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 434.94,
          "end": 437.4,
          "en": "So it's safe to do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 437.4,
          "end": 440.31,
          "en": "And we can set state.isAuthenticated",
